        <h2 id="variations">Budget, Long-Distance and Busy-Week Variations</h2>
        <p>
          The same wheels can be bent to fit your real life instead of an
          ideal one.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>On a tight budget:</strong> build every wheel from free or
            cheap entries (a sunset walk, a cook-together night, a library
            visit, a home theme night) so any result is affordable.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Long distance:</strong> share the wheel link on a video
            call and spin together. Good entries are a movie to start in sync,
            a recipe to cook on camera, an online game, or a conversation
            prompt.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Busy weeks with little time:</strong> add a duration to
            each entry, such as "20-minute walk" or "one episode and tea," so
            the wheel fits the evening you actually have.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Mixed tastes:</strong> use two wheels, one built by each of
            you, and alternate whose wheel gets spun each week.
          </li>
        </ul>

