        <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How many entries should I put on a date night wheel?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            For most date night decisions, 6 to 12 entries works best: enough
            variety to feel worth spinning, few enough that every option is one
            you both want. Bucket list and habit wheels can hold 20 to 30
            entries.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What if one of us doesn't like what the wheel picks?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            Only add options you are both genuinely fine with. If you want an
            escape hatch, agree on one veto each per session before spinning,
            and treat the spin after a veto as final.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Can we use separate wheels for different decisions in one night?
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            Yes. Build one wheel for the activity and another for food, save
            both as bookmarks, and spin each in turn. Every wheel you build has
            its own shareable link.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can we use a spin wheel for a long-distance relationship?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            Yes. Share the wheel link over a video call and spin together. Good
            entries include a movie to watch in sync, a recipe to cook on
            camera, an online game, or a conversation prompt.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Are there other wheels that work well for couples?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            Yes. A Yes or No wheel handles quick go or no-go calls, a coin flip
            wheel settles a tie between two options, and a number picker can
            decide who goes first or who pays.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do we need an account to build a date night wheel?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            No. You can build, spin and share a wheel by link without creating
            an account.
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="takeaways">
          <h2>✅ Key Takeaways</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              A wheel does not replace the thinking; it removes the last,
              tiring step of choosing between options you already accept.
            </li>
            <li>
              The 20 setups cover dinner, outings, nights in, romance and
              shared goals, each with entries ready to copy.
            </li>
            <li>
              Both partners should approve every entry, especially on personal
              wheels like forfeits and conversation prompts.
            </li>
            <li>
              Save wheels as bookmarks and agree the veto rule before you spin.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

